-- title:
--   Convergence of the canonical CFZ ratios beyond the small primes
-- statement:
--   Let $k\ge2$ and let $d$ be selected CFZ canonical-carry Fourier data of length $k$. Suppose $d.R\ge2$ and $d.w$ is at least the complex exceptional-prime bound of the W-tricked CFZ system. Then the canonical arithmetic-to-zeta local ratios indexed by primes $p>d.w$ are multipliable:
--   $$
--   \prod_{p>d.w}\mathcal R_{d,p}
--   $$
--   exists as an unordered complex product. The cutoff excludes the finite small-prime set; all the remaining parameters are those supplied by $d$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs/blob/8822f7ddef30fadbd92e1c6ab4ed897af356af5e/src/latest/Wikipedia/GreenTao/Sieve/CFZCanonicalCarryFourierNormalization.lean#L327-L364

